 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** Proposed by Niemeyer et al. in "Neural Scene Graphs for Dynamic Scenes" (CVPR 2021) [S1].
-*   **Development:** Builds upon implicit neural representations for static scenes (NeRF) [S1]. It extends differentiable rendering to dynamic scenes by introducing a hierarchical scene-graph model [S1].
-*   **Usage:** Used for novel view synthesis of dynamic scenes, 3D object detection, and modeling scenes with unseen object arrangements [S1].
+Neural Scene Graphs was introduced by Park et al. in 2021 [S1]. The method builds on the success of implicit neural representations for static scenes, specifically NeRF by Mildenhall et al. [22], and extends it to dynamic scenes by introducing a hierarchical scene-graph model [S1]. It addresses the limitation of existing methods that rely on static scenes with consistent mappings from a 3D point to a 2D observation [S1].
 
